-- Enemy paths, one row per polyline point, in map (image-pixel) space matching
-- the level art. point_index is travel order: point 0 is the spawn, the last is
-- the exit.
--
-- Lexington and Concord (path 0): the British advance -- enters at "To Boston"
-- (right), follows the road west through the S-curve past Lexington Green, up to
-- Concord, and out across the Old North Bridge (left). Hand-traced route,
-- centered on the road (tower-slot platforms excluded), smoothed with a
-- centripetal Catmull-Rom spline and arc-length resampled to evenly spaced
-- points for smooth enemy walking. Traced from images/lexington_and_concord.png.

-- Bunker Hill (two paths converging on the redoubt): path 0 lands at
-- Entrance 1 (south-west beach) and climbs the west road past Breed's Hill;
-- path 1 lands at Entrance 2 (south-east beach) and climbs the east road.
-- Both end at the fort gate (the EXIT). Same authoring pipeline as Lexington:
-- hand-traced, Catmull-Rom smoothed, arc-length resampled (~0.34px spacing).
-- Traced from images/level_002_bunker_hill.png.

-- Great Bridge (single path): the British column advances from the ENTRANCE
-- (east bank), crosses the wooden bridge over the Elizabeth River narrows, and
-- pushes up the causeway to the militia earthwork (EXIT, west). Path derived
-- directly from the road spline the art was drawn with (exact centerline).
